<title>
<![CDATA[ Mid Season Update! ]]>
</title>
<description>
<![CDATA[ Charlevoix, Nationals, Coupe de l'Avenir & Tour de l'Abitibi Femmes ]]>
</description>
<link>https://evetbuczkowski.substack.com/p/mid-season-update</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">https://evetbuczkowski.substack.com/p/mid-season-update</guid>
<dc:creator>
<![CDATA[ Eve Buczkowski ]]>
</dc:creator>
<pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 12:03:03 GMT</pubDate>
<enclosure url="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!1Ank!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F21d0b13d-a52a-421f-96c8-5336c8feb9da_2560x1707.webp" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/>
<content:encoded>
<![CDATA[ <p>Welcome back for another update!</p><p>It&#8217;s been a busy few months filled with racing across Quebec, plenty of climbing, lots of learning, and some of the most challenging racing I&#8217;ve experienced this season. From the climbs of Charlevoix, to Road Nationals, to a week-long stage race at Coupe de l&#8217;Avenir, and finishing off with Tour de l&#8217;Abitibi Femmes, it&#8217;s safe to say this summer has kept me busy.</p><p>As always, before getting into the racing, I want to say a huge thank you to my sponsors, coaches, teammates, family, and everyone who continues to support me. Every trip, training camp, and race is only possible because of the people who believe in me, and I&#8217;m incredibly grateful for all of the encouragement along the way.</p><p class="button-wrapper" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://evetbuczkowski.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}" data-component-name="ButtonCreateButton"><a class="button primary" href="https://evetbuczkowski.substack.com/subscribe?"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><div><hr></div><h2>Charlevoix Stage Race &#8211; Baie-Saint-Paul, Quebec</h2><p><strong>May 29th &#8211; 31st</strong></p><p>Charlevoix was the first major road stage race of the Canadian season, and it definitely lived up to its reputation. The courses are never easy, with constant climbing, technical roads, and very little opportunity to recover.</p><p>Going into the weekend, my role was to help make the racing hard for the field while also challenging myself against some of the strongest riders in Canada. The road race especially suited that objective, with the first half consisting of almost continuous climbing. It made for an aggressive race right from the start, and there was never really a moment where things settled down.</p><p>Although the results weren&#8217;t exactly the focus for me that weekend, I came away feeling stronger and more confident in my ability to handle long, difficult races. Every opportunity to race terrain like Charlevoix is valuable experience, and I left excited for the races still to come.</p><div class="image-gallery-embed" data-attrs="{&quot;gallery&quot;:{&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Race Ready!&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;staticGalleryImage&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/961dbb61-120c-48d3-9f9e-2fd5c83502e9_1456x474.png&quot;},&quot;images&quot;:[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/9cea5895-0bad-450a-9012-22ea652fff64_5712x4284.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/a71167db-19fb-4c03-a735-2031c05987d4_1500x2000.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/59614238-e4ac-441d-a399-a1a98e2f6622_1200x1600.jpeg&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;}]},&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true}"></div><div><hr></div><h2>Canadian Road National Championships &#8211; Beauce, Quebec</h2><p><strong>June 26th &#8211; 28th</strong></p><p>Road Nationals is always one of the biggest events on my calendar. Every province brings its strongest riders, everyone is aiming for the maple leaf jersey, and there&#8217;s an extra level of intensity that makes Nationals so special. This year brought an added challenge with plenty of rain throughout the weekend and a brand-new course that none of us had raced before. The wet roads demanded even more focus, especially through the pothole filled corners, and made every race a little more unpredictable.</p><p>Over the three events, I finished:</p><ul><li><p><strong>4th</strong> &#8211; Individual Time Trial</p></li><li><p><strong>7th</strong> &#8211; Road Race</p></li><li><p><strong>4th</strong> &#8211; Criterium</p></li></ul><p>While I was hoping for slightly stronger results, I&#8217;m proud of how I raced throughout the weekend. Nationals is always incredibly competitive, and every race highlighted areas I can continue improving while also giving me confidence that I&#8217;m moving in the right direction.</p><p>Racing in difficult conditions is something every cyclist has to learn to embrace, and this weekend was another reminder that adapting quickly and staying composed can make all the difference.</p><div class="image-gallery-embed" data-attrs="{&quot;gallery&quot;:{&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;My Favourites!&quot;,&quot;images&quot;:[{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/23bf7294-6d48-48a2-9cde-ef1c9053193c_5712x4284.jpeg&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;},{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/59f86d04-888f-4796-828b-0491a3da629a_5712x4284.jpeg&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/5fb66dcb-81f1-4c9d-b955-42cee1164219_1096x744.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/6eb0da3b-3db4-4ad2-8912-c02c42b5f49f_1179x836.jpeg&quot;}],&quot;staticGalleryImage&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/760aea48-aedd-4756-ab49-17f9796066da_1456x1456.png&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;}},&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true}"></div><div><hr></div><h2>Coupe de l&#8217;Avenir - Lachute, Quebec</h2><p><strong>July 1st - 5th</strong></p><p>Coupe de l&#8217;Avenir was one of the races I had been looking forward to all season. Going into the week, the original plan was to ride for the general classification myself, but as the race unfolded, our team tactics evolved.</p><p>Instead of focusing on my own GC ambitions, I shifted into more of a domestique role to help support my teammates in their fight for podiums and strong overall results. While it&#8217;s always fun to chase your own opportunities, being able to contribute to the team&#8217;s success is just as rewarding. Throughout the week our communication continued to improve, everyone committed fully to their roles, and we worked incredibly well together. Stage racing is demanding, not only physically but mentally, and having teammates you can trust makes a huge difference.</p><p>Personally, I was still happy to finish <strong>9th overall</strong>, especially considering the change in role during the race. One of my strongest rides came on Stage 4, where I finished just off the podium in 4th. More importantly, the week reminded me how much I enjoy racing as part of a team and how satisfying it is when everyone works together toward a common goal.</p><p>The racing was hard every single day, but our team kept spirits high throughout the week, making it one of my favourite events of the summer.</p><div class="image-gallery-embed" data-attrs="{&quot;gallery&quot;:{&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Race Pictures&quot;,&quot;images&quot;:[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/30d43239-f687-416a-a885-d583b9fbfe56_6240x4160.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/a473b911-dd10-47d4-bdf0-c1bd8ac995b7_6240x4160.jpeg&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;},{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/4fb3fa7d-1c31-413f-ad39-835e388d85e9_1179x779.jpeg&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;}],&quot;staticGalleryImage&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/1eaba38a-5bf3-4c89-a9cd-211ed3969d6e_1456x474.png&quot;}},&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true}"></div><div><hr></div><h2>Tour de l&#8217;Abitibi Femmes - Rouyn Noranda, Abitibi</h2><p><strong>July 10th - 13th</strong></p><p>The final race of this block was Tour de l&#8217;Abitibi Femmes, and it was an exciting way to finish off several weeks of racing. One of my favourite parts of this event was getting the opportunity to race against international competition. It&#8217;s always fun to line up against riders from different countries, and it adds another level to the racing experience.</p><p>The week started off really well with:</p><ul><li><p><strong>3rd</strong> on Stage 1</p></li><li><p><strong>5th</strong> on Stage 2</p></li></ul><p>Going into Stage 3, I was sitting in a strong position overall and feeling confident. Unfortunately, a combination of wrong wheel wrong time during the stage ended up costing me valuable time and ultimately took me out of contention for the general classification.</p><p>That was definitely disappointing, but stage racing is unpredictable, and sometimes things simply don&#8217;t go according to plan. I wanted to finish the race on a high note, and the final individual time trial gave me exactly that opportunity. I was able to ride to <strong>3rd place</strong>, which felt like a great redemption after the previous day&#8217;s disappointment.</p><p>I also finished <strong>2nd in the Sprint Competition</strong>, giving me another result to be proud of after a challenging week.</p><p>Despite the setbacks, I had an incredible time racing in Abitibi. The atmosphere, the competition, and the experience made it one of the highlights of my summer, and I learned a lot that I&#8217;ll carry into the rest of the season.</p><div class="image-gallery-embed" data-attrs="{&quot;gallery&quot;:{&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Borrowing the Sprint Jersey from Elodie!&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;images&quot;:[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/webp&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/21d0b13d-a52a-421f-96c8-5336c8feb9da_2560x1707.webp&quot;},{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/7f056ee9-ca6e-44da-8ef3-465dcbda7dd2_2560x1706.webp&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/webp&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/webp&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/347759a7-db99-490d-b39c-ccaf08c0aedd_2560x1707.webp&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/webp&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/2bd0e4a2-9bc5-42e0-adbb-b171042d0ce8_2560x1707.webp&quot;},{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/dc4d7a0f-65c7-4da7-9177-0fed93595608_2560x1707.webp&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/webp&quot;}],&quot;staticGalleryImage&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/731c630d-04de-4941-9be4-4783170ed04c_1456x1210.png&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;}},&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true}"></div><div><hr></div><h2>Looking Ahead &#8211; UCI Junior Track World Championships</h2><p>With my road block now complete, my focus is beginning to shift back toward the track and the UCI Junior Track World Championships in Belgium later this summer.</p><p>After several consecutive weeks of racing, I took a short period to recover before beginning the next phase of preparation. Sometimes recovery is just as important as training, and taking a step back for a few days has left me feeling refreshed and excited for what&#8217;s ahead.</p><p>Next week, I&#8217;ll be spending a few days training in Milton before heading to Bromont on <strong>August 4th</strong> for the final training camp held by John Malois leading into Worlds.</p><p>Representing Canada at the UCI Junior Track World Championships for the second consecutive year is an incredible opportunity, and I&#8217;m excited to continue building toward that goal. There is still plenty of work to do before Belgium, but I&#8217;m looking forward to getting back to the velodrome, putting in the final preparations with the team, and seeing what we can accomplish on the world stage.</p><h2>Thank You</h2><p>As always, thank you to everyone who continues to support me throughout this journey. Whether you&#8217;ve followed along on social media, cheered from the sidelines, helped behind the scenes, or made these trips possible through sponsorship, I truly appreciate every bit of encouragement.</p><p>This road season has brought plenty of highs, some setbacks, and countless lessons, but every race has helped me grow as both an athlete and a person. I&#8217;m excited for what&#8217;s next as I shift my focus back to the track and prepare to represent Canada once again in Belgium.</p><p>See you after Worlds!</p><p><strong>Eve</strong></p> ]]>
</content:encoded>
</item>
