<![CDATA[ Eve Buczkowski ]]>
</dc:creator>
<pubDate>Tue, 12 May 2026 10:03:20 GMT</pubDate>
<enclosure url="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!D1SP!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F72ccb37e-999a-4e57-91cf-1e94d1bcf1ac_1086x724.jpeg" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/>
<content:encoded>
<![CDATA[ <p>Welcome back for another update! This years track nationals experience was nothing short of amazing, and being able to get back on my road bike adds to the excitement! I can&#8217;t wait to show you all what I&#8217;ve been up to and what&#8217;s to come! A huge thank you to my sponsors, supporters, coaches, teammates, and family for helping make all of my trips possible. Your support allows me to continue pursuing my goals, travelling to races across the country, and developing as both an athlete and person. I&#8217;m incredibly grateful to have such an amazing group of people behind me every step of the way.</p><div class="subscription-widget-wrap-editor" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://evetbuczkowski.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}" data-component-name="SubscribeWidgetToDOM"><div class="subscription-widget show-subscribe"><div class="preamble"><p class="cta-caption">Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work!</p></div><form class="subscription-widget-subscribe"><input type="email" class="email-input" name="email" placeholder="Type your email&#8230;" tabindex="-1"><input type="submit" class="button primary" value="Subscribe"><div class="fake-input-wrapper"><div class="fake-input"></div><div class="fake-button"></div></div></form></div></div><h3><strong>Track Nationals 2026 - March 27th-29th, Edmonton, AB</strong></h3><p>Track Nationals this year was something special. Heading out to Edmonton for the 2026 Canadian U17/U19 Track National Championships for my last year as a U19 was an experience I&#8217;ll remember for a long time. Racing at the brand new Alberta Velodrome against the best junior riders in the country pushed me physically and mentally, and I&#8217;m really happy with how the weekend went overall.</p><div class="image-gallery-embed" data-attrs="{&quot;gallery&quot;:{&quot;images&quot;:[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/72ccb37e-999a-4e57-91cf-1e94d1bcf1ac_1086x724.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/c2b837b4-0256-4e0a-9216-592f964e78d2_1086x724.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/fbc27055-ac4b-4ce6-9a87-4d5f0bc29dda_2174x1446.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/7d38ec74-0b13-4a92-bba9-22476ce27633_1086x725.jpeg&quot;}],&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;staticGalleryImage&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/515efb3f-8dad-4a43-a510-ad977e636921_1456x1456.png&quot;}},&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true}"></div><p>From timed events like the Individual Pursuit and Kilo, to bunch races including the Scratch Race, Elimination, Points Race, and Madison, every event brought different challenges and opportunities to learn. Nationals always has a different atmosphere, faster racing, higher pressure, and incredible energy from riders, coaches, teammates, and supporters from all across Canada.</p><p>This weekend was packed with highs, personal improvements, and a lot of valuable experience. I&#8217;m proud of the rides I put together and especially proud of how I stayed consistent across such a busy schedule of events. My results were:</p><ul><li><p>3rd in IP</p></li><li><p>3rd in Scratch</p></li><li><p>2nd in Elimination</p></li><li><p>2nd in Points</p></li><li><p>2nd in Kilo (hitting Elite B standard as a Junior!)</p></li><li><p>3rd in Madison </p></li><li><p>1st in Team Pursuit (Representing Ontario)</p></li><li><p>2nd in Team Sprint (Representing Ontario)</p></li></ul><div class="image-gallery-embed" data-attrs="{&quot;gallery&quot;:{&quot;images&quot;:[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/7a4d6413-7c30-4c1b-b98b-9caffffec6ed_1086x725.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/22d8e685-789f-4eb2-9097-491dbdb70188_1086x724.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/639a66c3-46d2-466d-9d22-a7feb87bb212_1086x724.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/bb1a6e41-7a9b-41b8-a34a-c9fddfebe4e6_724x1084.jpeg&quot;}],&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;A snippet of race moments&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;staticGalleryImage&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/b100d328-1571-46b9-adc3-b3f93bc7547f_1456x1456.png&quot;}},&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true}"></div><p>One of the coolest parts of the weekend was getting to race team events with Team Ontario. Team Pursuit and Team Sprint are always exciting because they rely so heavily on trust, communication, and committing fully for your teammates. There&#8217;s something really rewarding about suffering together and chasing fast times as a group. Nationals weekends are never easy. Between warmups, cooldowns, qualifying rounds, recovery, and preparing mentally for the next race, it&#8217;s a constant cycle for multiple days straight, but those are the weekends that teach you the most, and I left Edmonton feeling motivated for what&#8217;s next.</p><div class="image-gallery-embed" data-attrs="{&quot;gallery&quot;:{&quot;images&quot;:[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/8d0da43e-fb4e-48a9-b094-3d1c9508d18f_725x1086.jpeg&quot;}],&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;My dad and I after I hit Elite B kilo standard&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;staticGalleryImage&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/8d0da43e-fb4e-48a9-b094-3d1c9508d18f_725x1086.jpeg&quot;}},&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true}"></div><p>Beyond the racing itself, one of my favourite parts of Nationals is always the people. Spending the weekend with teammates, coaches, friends, and competitors makes these trips so memorable. Whether it&#8217;s cheering each other on trackside, warming up together, or laughing after a long day of racing, those moments are just as important as the results.</p><p>I&#8217;m incredibly thankful for everyone who helped make this trip possible, my coaches, teammates, family, sponsors, and supporters. Your encouragement means so much and allows me to continue chasing bigger goals in the sport. This Nationals gave me a lot of confidence moving forward into the rest of the season. There are still so many areas I want to improve in, and this weekend only made me more motivated to keep pushing.</p><h3><strong>UCI Junior Track Worlds 2026 - Heusden-Zolder, Belgium from August 19th&#8211;23rd</strong></h3><p>After Nationals, I was selected to represent Canada again at the 2026 UCI Junior Track World Championships in Heusden-Zolder, Belgium from August 19th&#8211;23rd! I&#8217;m incredibly honoured to have been selected to Team Canada 2 years in a row and will be competing in the Team Pursuit, Elimination Race, and Points Race, while also being named as an alternate for the Scratch Race, Individual Pursuit, Omnium, and Madison. Competing on the world stage against the best junior riders internationally is an amazing opportunity, and I&#8217;m excited to continue learning, gaining experience, and representing Canada in Belgium this summer!</p><div class="image-gallery-embed" data-attrs="{&quot;gallery&quot;:{&quot;images&quot;:[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/29bb829d-b811-45c2-a95a-e9364629ac63_1084x724.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/f78938a2-6bc7-42f4-ba30-ef7008883f18_1084x724.jpeg&quot;}],&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;staticGalleryImage&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/013b2bf3-f017-4625-b2c2-13caeda56e75_1456x720.png&quot;}},&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true}"></div><h3><strong>What&#8217;s Next?</strong></h3><p>I am currently writing this update from Belgium on the Bill Buckley European Spring Project with Cycling Canada! So far I have done 3 races, May 2nd, 3rd, and 10th.. May 10th being the biggest one with over 150 girls! The next races include the team and I travelling to France later this week to race Tour du G&#233;vaudan Occitanie Femmes on May 16th and 17th! Updates about these races will be made in my next Substack at the beginning of June, see you then!</p><h3><strong>Charlevoix Stage Race &#8211; Baie-Saint-Paul, Quebec &#8212; May 29th - 31st</strong></h3><p>The Charlevoix Stage Race is coming up next on the calendar! This demanding three-day road race will be a great test of endurance, teamwork, tactics, and recovery. I&#8217;m really looking forward to racing alongside my teammates and taking on the challenging terrain. Last year was an incredible experience, and I&#8217;m excited to head back and see what we can accomplish this time around!</p><h3><strong>Road Nationals &#8211; Beauce, Quebec &#8212; June 26th - 28th</strong></h3><p>Road Nationals in Quebec will be one of the major highlights of my season. Competing against the top U19 riders from across Canada on demanding courses will be an exciting challenge and a great opportunity to put all of this season&#8217;s training and racing experience to the test. I&#8217;m looking forward to pushing myself, racing hard, and seeing what I can accomplish on the national stage.</p><h3><strong>Thank You to My Sponsors</strong></h3><p>Thank you again to all of my sponsors for your continued support throughout this season. Your generosity and belief in me allow me to travel, train, and compete at events across Canada while continuing to grow as an athlete. I&#8217;m incredibly grateful to represent such amazing people and organizations, and I&#8217;m excited to keep building on this season and chasing even bigger goals ahead.</p><p>Your support means everything, so thank you for being a part of my journey.</p><p>Eve</p><div class="subscription-widget-wrap-editor" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://evetbuczkowski.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}" data-component-name="SubscribeWidgetToDOM"><div class="subscription-widget show-subscribe"><div class="preamble"><p class="cta-caption">Thanks for reading Chasing the Break: My Journey in Cycling! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.</p></div><form class="subscription-widget-subscribe"><input type="email" class="email-input" name="email" placeholder="Type your email&#8230;" tabindex="-1"><input type="submit" class="button primary" value="Subscribe"><div class="fake-input-wrapper"><div class="fake-input"></div><div class="fake-button"></div></div></form></div></div> ]]>
