<![CDATA[ <p>Hello Everyone,</p><p>Welcome back for another update! The start of 2026 has been action packed on the track, and I&#8217;m excited to share how the first two months of the year have gone. Between C2 and Elite Nationals, Ontario Cups, NCIM Race Nights, and a Cycling Canada development camp, there&#8217;s been no shortage of racing, learning, and growth. As always, thank you to my 2026 sponsors for believing in me this season! I can&#8217;t wait to show you all what I&#8217;ve been up to and what&#8217;s to come! </p><h3>&#128680; Sponsor Announcement! </h3><p>A big thank you to <a href="https://www.dougtarryhomes.com/">Doug Tarry Homes</a>, <a href="https://www.wellingtonstreetfamilydentistry.com/">Dr.Candice Wakulich at Wellington Family Dentistry</a>, and <a href="http://2003foundation.org/">The Hamilton 2003 Foundation</a> for already supporting me early on in my season!!</p><div class="subscription-widget-wrap-editor" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://evetbuczkowski.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}" data-component-name="SubscribeWidgetToDOM"><div class="subscription-widget show-subscribe"><div class="preamble"><p class="cta-caption">Subscribe for free to receive new updates and support my journey!</p></div><form class="subscription-widget-subscribe"><input type="email" class="email-input" name="email" placeholder="Type your email&#8230;" tabindex="-1"><input type="submit" class="button primary" value="Subscribe"><div class="fake-input-wrapper"><div class="fake-input"></div><div class="fake-button"></div></div></form></div></div><div><hr></div><h1>January - Bromont, QC and Milton, ON</h1><h1>UCI C2 &#8211; Bromont, QC: 6th - 7th</h1><p>The season kicked off with the UCI C2 in Bromont. Racing against a fast international field was a great challenge and really tested my speed and tactics. It was exciting to start the year pushing hard on the track and learning from every lap.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ppY_!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F11c3904a-7758-46b2-af50-f9e1dd231f8d_1912x1530.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ppY_!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F11c3904a-7758-46b2-af50-f9e1dd231f8d_1912x1530.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ppY_!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F11c3904a-7758-46b2-af50-f9e1dd231f8d_1912x1530.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ppY_!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F11c3904a-7758-46b2-af50-f9e1dd231f8d_1912x1530.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ppY_!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F11c3904a-7758-46b2-af50-f9e1dd231f8d_1912x1530.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ppY_!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F11c3904a-7758-46b2-af50-f9e1dd231f8d_1912x1530.jpeg" width="532" height="425.6730769230769" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/11c3904a-7758-46b2-af50-f9e1dd231f8d_1912x1530.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1165,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:532,&quot;bytes&quot;:336551,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://evetbuczkowski.substack.com/i/190409189?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F11c3904a-7758-46b2-af50-f9e1dd231f8d_1912x1530.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ppY_!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F11c3904a-7758-46b2-af50-f9e1dd231f8d_1912x1530.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ppY_!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F11c3904a-7758-46b2-af50-f9e1dd231f8d_1912x1530.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ppY_!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F11c3904a-7758-46b2-af50-f9e1dd231f8d_1912x1530.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ppY_!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F11c3904a-7758-46b2-af50-f9e1dd231f8d_1912x1530.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw" loading="lazy"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class="image-caption">Me (Left) and my teammate Taylor Tompkins (Right) in the Madison!</figcaption></figure></div><p>Results:</p><ul><li><p>4th in Madison</p></li><li><p>18th Omnium</p></li></ul><h3>Canadian Elite &amp; Masters Track Nationals &#8211; Bromont, QC: 9th - 11th</h3><p>Right after, I lined up for Elite Nationals. Competing against Canada&#8217;s top U23 and elite riders as a U19, every race was a lesson in pacing, strategy, and mental focus. I came away feeling stronger and more confident in my racing abilities. Was definitely a fun couple days of racing. Taylor and I went into the Madison again, this time getting 3rd!</p><div class="image-gallery-embed" data-attrs="{&quot;gallery&quot;:{&quot;images&quot;:[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/fff79b22-b04c-4af7-9dcb-d7854193153e_2048x1630.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/43ae8154-09da-4023-86b7-85ba0c658e21_4284x5712.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/8fbe5fe3-0709-4a9d-983a-97f765062058_1036x798.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/afc4d878-f827-4901-984b-045e988f5420_1008x766.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/fed5c5f6-7f51-4f6c-b1d6-93b203af7a0f_1025x768.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/02b26925-61f0-4750-ba2b-3e981cccaeb6_1170x1560.jpeg&quot;}],&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Me in the IP, Scratch Race, and Madison! (Including Madison podium and Brody and I)&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;staticGalleryImage&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/10942e69-5a86-4383-a7cb-6b38921be72d_1456x964.png&quot;}},&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true}"></div><p> I&#8217;m very impressed with how I competed and had lots of fun while doing so!</p><p>Results:</p><ul><li><p>3rd Madison</p></li><li><p>5th Scratch Race</p></li><li><p>8th Individual Pursuit (4km, I usually do 3km)</p></li><li><p>10th Points Race</p></li><li><p>10th Kilo TT</p></li></ul><h3>Ontario Cup #2 &#8211; Milton, ON: 17th</h3><p>The second Ontario Cup of the year gave me another opportunity to put race tactics into practice. The sprints and endurance efforts were intense, and it was a great way to maintain race sharpness in between bigger track events.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!noBG!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4e124a63-3fa0-4bc9-9a4d-a8821bff9a82_4032x3024.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM