g 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!9QZ4!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b90ed5f-33bd-4187-b17e-71e679155d06_5712x4284.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw" loading="lazy"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class="image-caption">Lili (Left), Me (Middle), Addi (Right) - Kilo Podium!</figcaption></figure></div><h3>Provincial Championships &#8211; Milton, ON: 27th - March 1st</h3><p>The Provincial Track Championships wrapped up the month. Racing against the top riders in the province, every event demanded focus, determination, and commitment. It was a great way to test my early season form and see how far I&#8217;ve come. After being sick the week before, I am happy with how I competed but I am itching for more at Nationals in the end of March.</p><div class="image-gallery-embed" data-attrs="{&quot;gallery&quot;:{&quot;images&quot;:[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/2b040f4b-9e8d-45e0-b743-10c1471b5722_4032x3024.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/c6f695f6-0cd9-4e08-9388-d2219e2c75b7_4032x3024.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/12912c22-b1f3-4813-a2e8-6b0ed334016d_4032x3024.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/5da02d68-0db9-4de9-a3d1-617193ba4027_4032x3024.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/17050a78-9fdf-46f3-8c1a-36876a9cecb3_1170x1560.jpeg&quot;}],&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Podiums and Team Pursuit Lineup&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;staticGalleryImage&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/94a10433-5004-417d-9b51-1bd7d8cdc5a9_1456x1210.png&quot;}},&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true}"></div><p>Results:</p><ul><li><p>1st Kilo</p></li><li><p>1st IP</p></li><li><p>1st Omnium (Scratch, Tempo, Elimination, Points)</p></li><li><p>1st Team Pursuit</p></li></ul><p>Overall, a very successful start to my 2026 year! I can&#8217;t wait to see what I can do at Nationals in Edmonton!</p><div><hr></div><h3>Next Up!</h3><h3>Track Nationals &#8211; Edmonton, AB &#8212; March 27th - 29th</h3><p>Coming up soon is Track Nationals held in the brand new Alberta Velodrome. I&#8217;m looking forward to testing my speed and tactics against the best riders in the country once again. It&#8217;s a big opportunity to see how my training is paying off and to gain more racing experience as a developing rider.</p><h3>European Spring Project &#8211; Brussels, BEL + Lyons, FR &#8212; April 29th - May 18th</h3><p>I&#8217;m also heading to Europe for the Cycling Canada Spring Road Project, racing against some of the top juniors internationally and getting lots of experience on European roads over the course of 3 weeks! Competing in 2 UCI races will be an amazing experience to learn, grow, and push my limits for Canadian Road Nationals.</p><h3>Charlevoix Stage Race &#8211; Baie-Saint-Paul, Quebec &#8212; May 29th - 31st</h3><p>The Charlevoix Stage Race is next on the calendar. This multi-day road event will test endurance, tactics, and recovery over 3 consecutive days. I&#8217;m excited to race with my teammates and tackle the challenging course. Last year was a blast so I can&#8217;t wait to see what we have up our sleeve this year!</p><h3>Road Nationals &#8211; Beauce, Quebec &#8212; June 26th - 28th</h3><p>The season will hit a peak at Road Nationals in Quebec, one of the biggest events of the year. Racing against the top juniors (U19) from across the country on challenging courses will be a true test of endurance, tactics, and mental focus. I&#8217;m excited to see how the season&#8217;s training and early races have prepared me, and I can&#8217;t wait to give it everything on the road!</p><div><hr></div><h3>Thank You to My Sponsors</h3><p>I couldn&#8217;t do any of this without the support of my amazing sponsors. Thank you for helping me chase my goals, travel to races, and continue developing as a rider. All of your support is truly appreciated, and I can&#8217;t wait to show you what I have to offer this year!</p><p>Your support means everything, so thank you for being a part of my journey.</p><p>Eve</p><p></p> ]]>
