reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><div><hr></div><h3>Track Season Highlights</h3><p>I kicked off the year on the track with strong results at Ontario Cup events, collecting podiums in scratch, elimination, and other endurance races and proving the work over the winter was paying off. The real breakthrough came at the U17/Junior Canadian Track Championships in Milton leaving the track with so many incredible memories. I was fortunate to earn:</p><ul><li><p>&#129351; Gold in the Junior Women Elimination Race</p></li><li><p>&#129352; Silver in the Individual Pursuit (and briefly set a world record level time in qualifying)</p></li><li><p>&#129353; Podium finishes in other events including scratch and kilo </p></li><li><p>&#129351; Contributed to strong team performances in Team Pursuit and Madison for Team Ontario &#127464;&#127462; </p></li></ul><p>Being surrounded by such talent, teammates and rivals alike, all chasing big things  made every session and every race feel more meaningful.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h44V!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F100947f5-5c41-418d-9f38-219cbfd3813c_2820x2820.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h44V!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F100947f5-5c41-418d-9f38-219cbfd3813c_2820x2820.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h44V!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F100947f5-5c41-418d-9f38-219cbfd3813c_2820x2820.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h44V!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F100947f5-5c41-418d-9f38-219cbfd3813c_2820x2820.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h44V!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F100947f5-5c41-418d-9f38-219cbfd3813c_2820x2820.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h44V!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F100947f5-5c41-418d-9f38-219cbfd3813c_2820x2820.jpeg" width="494" height="494" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/100947f5-5c41-418d-9f38-219cbfd3813c_2820x2820.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1456,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:494,&quot;bytes&quot;:1974268,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://evetbuczkowski.substack.com/i/182886335?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F100947f5-5c41-418d-9f38-219cbfd3813c_2820x2820.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h44V!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F100947f5-5c41-418d-9f38-219cbfd3813c_2820x2820.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h44V!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F100947f5-5c41-418d-9f38-219cbfd3813c_2820x2820.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h44V!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F100947f5-5c41-418d-9f38-219cbfd3813c_2820x2820.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!h44V!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F100947f5-5c41-418d-9f38-219cbfd3813c_2820x2820.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><div><hr></div><h3>Representing Canada on the World Stage</h3><p>A huge milestone for me this season was being selected to represent Canada at the 2025 UCI Junior Track World Championships in Apeldoorn, Netherlands. Riding with the Canadian junior track team was a dream come true and a glimpse into the level it takes to compete globally with the best young riders in the world. Travel obstacles (thanks Air Canada strikes &#128517;) made it an adventure before the racing even began, but once we arrived, it was full focus on training and getting ready to race.</p><div class="image-gallery-embed" data-attrs="{&quot;gallery&quot;:{&quot;images&quot;:[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/948ce28d-0d3e-424d-9eea-dec1c9bf37e8_1803x1352.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/5a584091-b2e4-4156-b49f-dc0644b049de_1491x1118.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/1b5299b6-10ca-46de-9907-d318ee03876e_1080x810.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/e7a916ca-98da-4882-9c89-b13174bbac88_1821x1366.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/a5a7ab80-2dba-4610-adc4-1e3ae89fb1b0_1752x1314.jpeg&quot;}],&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;staticGalleryImage&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/04ebb96b-85f7-4232-a9b5-70303d43e927_1456x1210.png&quot;}},&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true}"></div><div><hr></div><h3>Road Season &#8212; National Championships &amp; U19 Racing</h3><p>Transitioning into the road season, I continued to challenge myself with distance and competition. At Canadian Road Nationals in St-Georges, Quebec, I lined up with the best juniors in the country, fought hard in criterium and road race conditions, and finished proud wearing Ontario colours. Other highlights this summer included racing in the Tour de l&#8217;Abitibi F&#233;minin, a UCI Junior Nations Cup race that was not only competitive but historic for women&#8217;s junior cycling in Canada. Getting the chance to line up against international teams was unreal and a reminder of how much potential there is in North American junior racing. </p><p>Results:</p><ul><li><p>4th National Road Race</p></li><li><p>6th National ITT</p></li><li><p>3rd l&#8217;Abitibi F&#233;minin ITT</p></li><li><p>7th l&#8217;Abitibi GC</p></li><li><p>11th Charlevoix GC - U23/Elite Women</p></li></ul><div class="image-gallery-embed" data-attrs="{&quot;gallery&quot;:{&quot;images&quot;:[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/80ba65fe-6aa7-4304-a72d-f67b8464a9bb_4624x3468.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/1dc6e96d-3b9e-41a0-86a2-c20bbbd23770_3840x5120.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/97619302-f035-40a8-ab28-a003d5501a39_5120x3840.jpeg&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/4da7aa97-8fad-4e8e-80bd-f531b70cab85_4451x3338.jpeg&quot;}],&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;staticGalleryImage&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/dafa0384-ab12-4d4a-b7b4-2b872e6c923e_1456x1456.png&quot;}},&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true}"></div><div><hr></div><h3>What 2025 Taught Me</h3><p>This season was a mix of racing hard and learning harder. I&#8217;ve learned:</p><ul><li><p>Consistency in training pays off, even when results don&#8217;t show immediately.</p></li><li><p>Community matters, teammates, coaches, family, and volunteers make every result possible.</p></li><li><p>Growth often happens in the moments we least expect, like travel chaos or tough weather days.</p></li></ul><p>Looking back on these highs and lows, I feel more motivated than ever heading into the 2026 season.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6hEX!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe65c6ceb-9a14-4cde-ad95-29c098de78b2_4032x3024.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6hEX!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe65c6ceb-9a14-4cde-ad95-29c098de78b2_4032x3024.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6hEX!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe65c6ceb-9a14-4cde-ad95-29c098de78b2_4032x3024.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6hEX!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe65c6ceb-9a14-4cde-ad95-29c098de78b2_4032x3024.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6hEX!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe65c6ceb-9a14-4cde-ad95-29c098de78b2_4032x3024.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6hEX!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe65c6ceb-9a14-4cde-ad95-29c098de78b2_4032x3024.jpeg" width="469" height="625.2259615384615" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/e65c6ceb-9a14-4cde-ad95-29c098de78b2_4032x3024.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1941,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:469,&quot;bytes&quot;:4947116,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://evetbuczkowski.substack.com/i/182886335?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe65c6ceb-9a14-4cde-ad95-29c098de78b2_4032x3024.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6hEX!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe65c6ceb-9a14-4cde-ad95-29c098de78b2_4032x3024.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6hEX!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe65c6ceb-9a14-4cde-ad95-29c098de78b2_4032x3024.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6hEX!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe65c6ceb-9a14-4cde-ad95-29c098de78b2_4032x3024.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6hEX!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe65c6ceb-9a14-4cde-ad95-29c098de78b2_4032x3024.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw" loading="lazy"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><div><hr></div><h3>Next Up!</h3><p>I&#8217;m already excited about 2026, bigger races, stronger teammates, and more chances to race internationally:</p><ul><li><p><strong>UCI C2 Track Racing &#8211; January 6-7 - Bromont, QC &#9989;</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Elite Track Nationals &#8211; January 9-11 - Bromont, QC &#9989;</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Track Provincials &#8211; March - Milton, ON</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Track Nationals &#8211; April - Milton, ON</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Southwest Block (Redlands Bicycle Classic + Gila UCI 2.2 or Bloom UCI 2.2) - April - California, USA</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Canadian Road Nationals - June - Beauce, QC</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Western Europe Kermesse Block - July - TBD</strong></p></li></ul><p>I can&#8217;t wait to keep building on everything I learned during my year of racing and continue improving as a rider. Each race and training block is another step toward bigger goals, and I&#8217;m ready to give it my all.</p><div><hr></div><h3>Thank you to my support team</h3><p>None of this would have been possible without the incredible support I&#8217;ve received this year. To my family, who drive the miles, calm the nerves, and celebrates every moment, thank you for believing in me before I even believed in myself. To my coaches and teammates, thank you for pushing me, for every interval, every lesson, and every laugh along the way. You&#8217;re the reason training feels like home. A massive thank you to my sponsors and supporters, your contributions help cover the realities of racing at this level: travel, equipment, food, and the freedom to focus fully on training and performance. Your support isn&#8217;t just appreciated, it&#8217;s what makes these dreams possible. I&#8217;m proud to represent you each time I ride. To everyone who cheers from the sidelines, messages encouragement, or simply follows along, I feel your support every step of the way and it truly means the world.</p><div><hr></div><h3>Future Support</h3><p>In 2026, I am grateful to have the opportunity to work with the 2003 Hamilton Cycling Foundation and Doug Tarry Homes to help offset the costs of being an elite athlete in todays world! If you are interested in supporting my journey send me an email and we can chat! </p><p>See you in 2026!</p><p>Eve</p><p></p><div class="subscription-widget-wrap-editor" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://evetbuczkowski.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}" data-component-name="SubscribeWidgetToDOM"><div class="subscription-widget show-subscribe"><div class="preamble"><p class="cta-caption">Thanks for reading Chasing the Break: My Journey in Cycling! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.</p></div><form class="subscription-widget-subscribe"><input type="email" class="email-input" name="email" placeholder="Type your email&#8230;" tabindex="-1"><input type="submit" class="button primary" value="Subscribe"><div class="fake-input-wrapper"><div class="fake-input"></div><div class="fake-button"></div></div></form></div></div> ]]>
