<![CDATA[ <p><strong>Hello Everyone,</strong></p><p>Welcome back for the MEGA UPDATE! It&#8217;s been a really busy 6 weeks on the bike. Probably the biggest racing block of the year with 12 race days, National and UCI events peppered in amongst some local and provincial races.</p><p>As you know, I&#8217;ve started a GoFundMe Campaign to financially support the most expensive portion of the racing year: <strong>representing Team Canada at the UCI Junior Track World Championships in Apeldoorn, Netherlands</strong>. If you&#8217;d like to help click the button below! Thank you so much to all the people who have already contributed, I&#8217;m over 80% of my goal so far. You can see how I&#8217;ve been using the proceeds of these funds at the end of this post.</p><p class="button-wrapper" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://www.gofundme.com/f/jr-track-worlds-apeldoorn-netherlands?attribution_id=sl:36f64f67-c365-40fd-9eff-a8480ff04d8c&amp;lang=en_US&amp;ts=1749506140&amp;utm_campaign=fp_sharesheet&amp;utm_content=amp13_c-amp14_c&amp;utm_medium=customer&amp;utm_source=copy_link&amp;v=amp14_c&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Contribute to my trip!&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}" data-component-name="ButtonCreateButton"><a class="button primary" href="https://www.gofundme.com/f/jr-track-worlds-apeldoorn-netherlands?attribution_id=sl:36f64f67-c365-40fd-9eff-a8480ff04d8c&amp;lang=en_US&amp;ts=1749506140&amp;utm_campaign=fp_sharesheet&amp;utm_content=amp13_c-amp14_c&amp;utm_medium=customer&amp;utm_source=copy_link&amp;v=amp14_c"><span>Contribute to my trip!</span></a></p><p>In this post, I&#8217;m excited to share updates from the finale of my outdoor road season, along with a look at my current training routine and how everything is building toward Junior Track World Championships at the end of August. Every achievement I make is made possible by your belief in me, and I want to ensure you&#8217;re always kept in the loop about how your support is making a real impact.</p><p>If we haven&#8217;t been able to connect yet, please feel free to reach out!</p><p>Thank you again for being a part of this journey. Let&#8217;s dive into the latest updates!</p><div><hr></div><h3>Canadian Road Nationals &#8211; June 27 to June 30, 2025 &#8211; Beauce, QC</h3><p>Nationals was definitely one of the hardest races I&#8217;ve done so far this season. Between the super strong field, the hilly courses, and the tough weather, it really pushed me, but it was also one of the best learning experiences I&#8217;ve had. </p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!J48d!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F745f1cd9-b851-4538-b484-90250c197602_3024x3108.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!J48d!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F745f1cd9-b851-4538-b484-90250c197602_3024x3108.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!J48d!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F745f1cd9-b851-4538-b484-90250c197602_3024x3108.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!J48d!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F745f1cd9-b851-4538-b484-90250c197602_3024x3108.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!J48d!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F745f1cd9-b851-4538-b484-90250c197602_3024x3108.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!J48d!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F745f1cd9-b851-4538-b484-90250c197602_3024x3108.jpeg" width="720" height="740" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/745f1cd9-b851-4538-b484-90250c197602_3024x3108.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:3108,&quot;width&quot;:3024,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:720,&quot;bytes&quot;:2899965,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://evetbuczkowski.substack.com/i/168864454?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F25144d1f-b5e5-40f7-841e-10b0f2cbc125_4032x3024.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!J48d!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F745f1cd9-b851-4538-b484-90250c197602_3024x3108.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!J48d!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F745f1cd9-b851-4538-b484-90250c197602_3024x3108.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!J48d!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F745f1cd9-b851-4538-b484-90250c197602_3024x3108.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!J48d!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F745f1cd9-b851-4538-b484-90250c197602_3024x3108.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw" loading="lazy"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class="image-caption">Me and Teags (left) - She got the call up to join the team at Track Worlds!</figcaption></figure></div><p>I raced the time trial, road race, and crit, ending up with two results I&#8217;m proud of:<br><strong>6th in the ITT</strong> <strong>-</strong> <strong>16km</strong></p><p><strong>4th in the road race</strong></p><p>The road race was especially challenging. It was cold, rainy, and windy, and the course had lots of climbing. I stayed focused, raced smart, and gave it everything I had to finish strong. Two world class riders were off the front and I finished the race with a strong sprint in the chase group. Nationals gave me a big confidence boost and showed me what I&#8217;m capable of when I really commit. The road race result was not what I wanted to get out of the weekend, but it leaves me determined and even more motivated for what&#8217;s to come next year. </p><div><hr></div><h3><strong>Montr&#233;al 2026 Worlds Course Recon &#8211; July 2, 2025 &#8211; Montr&#233;al, QC</strong></h3><p>While I was still in Qu&#233;bec, I got the chance to ride the 2026 World Championships course in Montr&#233;al with Cycling Canada and some of the EF Education Oatly pro riders. It was a police escorted ride through downtown Montr&#233;al in the middle of rush hour (sorry!) and felt super cool to be part of an event with such high caliber riders.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7MWU!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Feddc9dfe-0b6c-439a-8a83-b50c15a21f30_2803x2762.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7MWU!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Feddc9dfe-0b6c-439a-8a83-b50c15a21f30_2803x2762.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7MWU!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Feddc9dfe-0b6c-439a-8a83-b50c15a21f30_2803x2762.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7MWU!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Feddc9dfe-0b6c-439a-8a83-b50c15a21f30_2803x2762.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7MWU!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Feddc9dfe-0b6c-439a-8a83-b50c15a21f30_2803x2762.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7MWU!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Feddc9dfe-0b6c-439a-8a83-b50c15a21f30_2803x2762.jpeg" width="712" height="701.585444166964" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/eddc9dfe-0b6c-439a-8a83-b50c15a21f30_2803x2762.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:2762,&quot;width&quot;:2803,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:712,&quot;bytes&quot;:1546692,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://evetbuczkowski.substack.com/i/168864454?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8430c097-6a2b-4125-8341-c516303fd5d4_4032x3024.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7MWU!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Feddc9dfe-0b6c-439a-8a83-b50c15a21f30_2803x2762.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7MWU!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Feddc9dfe-0b6c-439a-8a83-b50c15a21f30_2803x2762.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7MWU!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Feddc9dfe-0b6c-439a-8a83-b50c15a21f30_2803x2762.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7MWU!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Feddc9dfe-0b6c-439a-8a83-b50c15a21f30_2803x2762.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw" loading="lazy"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class="image-caption">Riders at the future start line of the 2026 World Championship course</figcaption></figure></div><p>The course was awesome, pretty technical with some punchy climbs, and its amazing to imagine what it&#8217;ll look like when the Worlds happen next year. I&#8217;m super grateful I got to pre-ride it, and hopefully I&#8217;ll be back next year to race it!</p><div><hr></div><h3><strong>Mardis Lachine &#8211; July 1, 2025 &#8211; Montr&#233;al, QC</strong></h3><p>I did my first ever Mardis Lachine crit in Montreal and it was loads of fun. It also happened to be the first time they ever ran a dedicated women&#8217;s race! The race was fast, the course was really smooth and slightly technical, and the overall atmosphere was amazing for a regular Tuesday night. There were tons of strong riders in the field including the recently crowned Elite National champion and it made for a super exciting race.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!X3ds!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa24a1b4f-e6fd-4805-97bd-ae7d47e26014_3024x2385.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!X3ds!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa24a1b4f-e6fd-4805-97bd-ae7d47e26014_3024x2385.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!X3ds!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa24a1b4f-e6fd-4805-97bd-ae7d47e26014_3024x2385.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!X3ds!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa24a1b4f-e6fd-4805-97bd-ae7d47e26014_3024x2385.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!X3ds!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa24a1b4f-e6fd-4805-97bd-ae7d47e26014_3024x2385.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!X3ds!,w_2400,c_lim