<![CDATA[ <div class="subscription-widget-wrap-editor" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://evetbuczkowski.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}" data-component-name="SubscribeWidgetToDOM"><div class="subscription-widget show-subscribe"><div class="preamble"><p class="cta-caption">Feel free to subscribe to Chasing the Break: My Journey in Cycling!</p></div><form class="subscription-widget-subscribe"><input type="email" class="email-input" name="email" placeholder="Type your email&#8230;" tabindex="-1"><input type="submit" class="button primary" value="Subscribe"><div class="fake-input-wrapper"><div class="fake-input"></div><div class="fake-button"></div></div></form></div></div><p><strong>Hello Everyone,</strong></p><p>Welcome back! Over the past few months, I&#8217;ve had the opportunity to speak with many community-minded organizations about supporting my journey, and this is my chance to give you insight into how your support is being used. As always, I want to take a moment to express my deepest gratitude for your ongoing support. Your partnership means the world to me and plays a crucial role in helping me push my limits and achieve my goals on and off the bike.</p><p>Importantly, this month I started a GoFundMe Campaign to financially support the most expensive portion of the racing year: representing Team Canada at the UCI Junior Track World Championships in Apeldoorn, Netherlands. If you&#8217;d like to help click the button below! Thank you so much to all the people who have already contributed!</p><p class="button-wrapper" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://gofund.me/12a6af4b&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Contribute to my trip!&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}" data-component-name="ButtonCreateButton"><a class="button primary" href="https://gofund.me/12a6af4b"><span>Contribute to my trip!</span></a></p><p></p><p>In this post, I&#8217;m excited to share updates from a big month of racing in May, along with a look at my current training routine and how everything is building toward Canadian Road Nationals at the end of June. Every achievement I make is made possible by your belief in me, and I want to ensure you&#8217;re always kept in the loop about how your support is making a real impact.</p><p>If we haven&#8217;t been able to connect yet, please feel free to reach out!</p><p>Thank you again for being a part of this journey. Let&#8217;s dive into the latest updates!</p><div><hr></div><h3>Charlevoix Grand Prix &#8211; May 30 to June 1, 2025 &#8211; Charlevoix, QC</h3><p>The Charlevoix Grand Prix was one of the toughest races I&#8217;ve done so far this season, and it pushed me to a new level. Spanning three days and four stages, the event featured a mix of disciplines: a criterium, time trial, hill climb, and road race, each one testing a different aspect of racing. It was a huge learning experience, and I&#8217;m proud to say I finished 11th overall out of 85 Elite Women in the General Classification. </p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XQPA!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe73a3a52-4297-4bb8-a640-605349417363_1628x2048.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XQPA!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe73a3a52-4297-4bb8-a640-605349417363_1628x2048.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XQPA!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe73a3a52-4297-4bb8-a640-605349417363_1628x2048.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XQPA!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe73a3a52-4297-4bb8-a640-605349417363_1628x2048.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XQPA!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe73a3a52-4297-4bb8-a640-605349417363_1628x2048.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XQPA!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe73a3a52-4297-4bb8-a640-605349417363_1628x2048.jpeg" width="452" height="568.7252747252747" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/e73a3a52-4297-4bb8-a640-605349417363_1628x2048.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1832,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:452,&quot;bytes&quot;:475363,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://evetbuczkowski.substack.com/i/165564072?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe73a3a52-4297-4bb8-a640-605349417363_1628x2048.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XQPA!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe73a3a52-4297-4bb8-a640-605349417363_1628x2048.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XQPA!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe73a3a52-4297-4bb8-a640-605349417363_1628x2048.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XQPA!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe73a3a52-4297-4bb8-a640-605349417363_1628x2048.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XQPA!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe73a3a52-4297-4bb8-a640-605349417363_1628x2048.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw" loading="lazy"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Photo Credits: @sbreau.photography on Instagram</p><p>One of the biggest challenges was the weather, it was cold, raining, and windy every single day. Staying warm between stages was tough and racing in wet conditions made some technical sections slippery and mentally exhausting. It added an extra layer of difficulty to an already demanding course, and I had to stay really focused and tough through it all. </p><p>Here&#8217;s how each stage went:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Criterium</strong> &#8211; 24th</p></li><li><p><strong>Time Trial</strong> &#8211; 9th</p></li><li><p><strong>Hill Climb</strong> &#8211; 8th</p></li><li><p><strong>Road Race</strong> &#8211; 15th</p></li></ul><p>The road race on the final day was especially intense: 83km with 1,100m of elevation, completed in just under 2 hours and 20 minutes. The course was relentless, with constant rolling hills and sharp elevation gains, but I dug deep and stayed focused the entire time. It was a major physical and mental test, and I left the weekend feeling stronger and more prepared for what&#8217;s ahead.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!LzKN!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0aaac57e-2e57-42eb-95ec-0f27293fb26b_2000x1600.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!LzKN!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0aaac57e-2e57-42eb-95ec-0f27293fb26b_2000x1600.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!LzKN!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0aaac57e-2e57-42eb-95ec-0f27293fb26b_2000x1600.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!LzKN!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/http