<![CDATA[ <p><strong>Hello Everyone,</strong></p><p>I&#8217;m thrilled to welcome you to this special update from Eve Buczkowski, a U19 cyclist racing for Canada&#8217;s only women&#8217;s development team, Milton Revolution U23 Project. Over the past few months, I&#8217;ve had the opportunity to speak with many community minded organizations about supporting my journey, and this is my chance to give you insight into how your support is being used. As always, I want to take a moment to express my deepest gratitude for your ongoing support. Your partnership means the world to me and plays a crucial role in helping me push my limits and achieve my goals on and off the bike.</p><div class="subscription-widget-wrap-editor" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://evetbuczkowski.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}" data-component-name="SubscribeWidgetToDOM"><div class="subscription-widget show-subscribe"><div class="preamble"><p class="cta-caption">Thanks for reading Chasing the Break: My Journey in Cycling! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.</p></div><form class="subscription-widget-subscribe"><input type="email" class="email-input" name="email" placeholder="Type your email&#8230;" tabindex="-1"><input type="submit" class="button primary" value="Subscribe"><div class="fake-input-wrapper"><div class="fake-input"></div><div class="fake-button"></div></div></form></div></div><p>In this post, I&#8217;m excited to share insights on my journey as a young aspiring athlete with updates on recent races, a look into my training progress, and a view into how your support is helping me reach new milestones. Every achievement I make is made possible by your belief in me, and I want to ensure you&#8217;re always kept in the loop about how your investment is making an impact.</p><p>If we haven&#8217;t been able to connect yet, please feel free to reach out!</p><p>Thank you again for being a part of this journey. Let&#8217;s dive into the latest updates!</p><div><hr></div><h3>Spring Training &#8211; Outdoor Rides, LCW Racing &amp; Road Nationals Prep</h3><p>With the warmer weather finally arriving in Ontario, I&#8217;ve been spending more time training outdoors, which has been such a boost both physically and mentally. From long endurance rides in the countryside to short punchy intervals, it&#8217;s been great to feel the sun, push my limits, and build towards road season goals.</p><p>I&#8217;ve also been racing with the London Centennial Wheelers (LCW) during their weekly local events. Tuesday night races and Thursday time trials have been awesome ways to get race intensity in and sharpen my skills in a competitive but supportive environment. These sessions have helped me fine tune tactics and pacing, especially as I start focusing on Road Nationals coming up this June in Beauce, QC. Right now, I&#8217;m deep into training for that, putting in over 12 hours a week on the bike and doing everything I can to be at my best for one of the most important events of the year.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xZ-r!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd66154e3-8709-4fff-888a-9cbf58fbd28d_4032x3024.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xZ-r!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd66154e3-8709-4fff-888a-9cbf58fbd28d_4032x3024.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xZ-r!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd66154e3-8709-4fff-888a-9cbf58fbd28d_4032x3024.jpeg 848w, https://s