<![CDATA[ <p></p><p class="button-wrapper" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://evetbuczkowski.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}" data-component-name="ButtonCreateButton"><a class="button primary" href="https://evetbuczkowski.substack.com/subscribe?"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><h2>Thanks for Reading</h2><p>Hello Everyone,</p><p>I&#8217;m thrilled to welcome you to this special update from Eve Buczkowski, a U19 cyclist racing for Canada&#8217;s only women&#8217;s development team, Milton Revolution U23 Project.. Over the past few months, I&#8217;ve had the opportunity to speak with many community-minded organizations about supporting my journey and this is my chance to give you insight into how your support is being used. As always, I want to take a moment to express my deepest gratitude for your ongoing support. Your partnership means the world to me and plays a crucial role in helping me push my limits and achieve my goals on and off the bike.</p><p>In this post, I&#8217;m excited to share my life as a young aspiring athlete with updates on recent races, a look into my training progress, and insights into how your support is helping me reach new milestones. Every achievement I make is made possible by your belief in me, and I want to ensure you&#8217;re always kept in the loop about how your investment is making an impact.</p><p>Thank you again for being a part of this journey. Let&#8217;s dive into the latest updates!</p><h2>Ontario Track Academy - Milton, ON</h2><p>I can&#8217;t believe it's been two years since I joined the Ontario Track Academy (OTA), and I wanted to take a moment to reflect on how much it&#8217;s helped shape both my cycling performance and personal development.</p><p>The OTA has been a game-changer for me. The program&#8217;s high-performance coaching and positive training environment have pushed me to new limits on the bike. From refining my technique on the track to improving my strength off the bike, I&#8217;ve seen massive growth in my results at competitions. But it&#8217;s not just about the physical training&#8212;the mental and tactical aspects have also been key in helping me perform at my best under pressure.</p><p>Off the bike, the Academy has given me the support and discipline to balance training with my other commitments. The coaching staff has instilled in me a mindset of resilience and focus, and I&#8217;ve learned how to take care of my body and mind as an athlete, ensuring I stay in top form. For instance this month I met with my mental performance coach Judy Goss to discuss the mental aspect of being a high performance athlete. We talked about positive visualization and strategies to help cope with the stresses of race days, which I implemented during nationals.</p><p>I'm incredibly grateful for the opportunity to be part of such an inspiring and supportive community. Here&#8217;s to continuing this journey with the OTA and seeing where it takes me next!</p><p></p><h2>February 28 &#8594; March 2 - Track Provincials - Milton, ON</h2><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hxv4!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff4cc5c8b-2049-476d-84de-c49217edd28a_4032x3024.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hxv4!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff4cc5c8b-2049-476d-84de-c49217edd28a_4032x3024.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hxv4!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff4cc5c8b-2049-476d-84de-c49217edd28a_4032x3024.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hxv4!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff4cc5c8b-2049-476d-84de-c49217edd28a_4032x3024.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hxv4!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff4cc5c8b-2049-476d-84de-c49217edd28a_4032x3024.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hxv4!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff4cc5c8b-2049-476d-84de-c49217edd28a_4032x3024.jpeg" width="390" height="519.9107142857143" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/f4cc5c8b-2049-476d-84de-c49217edd28a_4032x3024.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1941,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:390,&quot;bytes&quot;:2043091,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://evetbuczkowski.substack.com/i/160891542?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff4cc5c8b-2049-476d-84de-c49217edd28a_4032x3024.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hxv4!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff4cc5c8b-2049-476d-84de-c49217edd28a_4032x3024.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hxv4!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff4cc5c8b-2049-476d-84de-c49217edd28a_4032x3024.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hxv4!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff4cc5c8b-2049-476d-84de-c49217edd28a_4032x3024.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hxv4!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff4cc5c8b-2049-476d-84de-c49217edd28a_4032x3024.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw" loading="lazy"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>My first Track Cycling Provincials as a first-year U19 rider was a memorable experience filled with learning, growth, and some big breakthroughs. Going into the weekend, my main goal was to gain experience and see how I stacked up against a strong field&#8212;but I came out of it with some major results I'm really proud of. I earned gold in the Kilo with a time of 1:15.139, averaging 47.911 km/h, which felt like one of my most powerful efforts at that time. I also won the Elimination Race, which was super tactical and demanded focus and timing every lap. Another major highlight was taking silver in the Individual Pursuit with a time of 3:47.955, averaging 47.378 km/h for 3 kilometers&#8212;good enough to hit the Canadian Junior A Standard, a key requirement for making it to the World Championships. That was a huge personal milestone and something I&#8217;ve been working toward. Over the weekend, I learned a lot about race strategy, pacing, and how to manage my energy across multiple events in an Omnium format. This experience definitely fueled my motivation, and I&#8217;m excited to keep building on this momentum as the season goes on. Huge thanks to my coaches, teammates, and everyone who supported me&#8212;I couldn&#8217;t have asked for a better first provincials</p><h2>March 10 &#8594; 15 - March Break Track Camp - Milton, ON</h2><p>Over March Break, I had the opportunity to attend an intensive training camp focused on team pursuit and team sprint, and it ended up being one of the most valuable blocks of training I&#8217;ve done so far. We spent the week dialling in technique, communication, and timing&#8212;key elements for success in both team events. In the team pursuit sessions, I really focused on pacing consistency, smooth exchanges, and maintaining speed through the line, all while syncing up with my teammates. It was amazing to feel the group come together and build that rhythm lap after lap. In the team sprint efforts, I worked on explosive starts, holding top-end speed, and clean transitions to keep the momentum flowing. The camp pushed me physically and mentally, but it also gave me a huge confidence boost in riding with a team and understanding the mechanics of these events at a deeper level. I left the week feeling stronger, more connected with my teammates, and more prepared for team events leading up to Track Nationals. </p><h2>April 4 &#8594; 6 - Track Nationals - Milton, ON</h2><p>Nationals was an absolutely unforgettable experience and easily the highlight of my season so far. One of the biggest moments came in the Individual Pursuit, where I held a <strong>world record</strong> time for the 3km&#8212;finishing in 3:42.648 at an average speed of 48.507 km/h, over a five second improvement from just a month earlier at Provincials.  It was a surreal feeling to be riding at that pace, knowing every lap was on the edge, and crossing the line with that time is something I&#8217;ll never forget. The world record only held for about 7 minutes when a fellow Team Ontario rider bested it. I also took the win in the Elimination Race, which really tested my race smarts, positioning, and ability to stay composed under pressure. Another highlight was winning the Team Pursuit with an amazing group of girls&#8212;our chemistry and trust made it such a strong and rewarding performance. But the most special moment might have been winning the Madison while wearing my hometown jersey from Railway City Cycling Club. Taking the top step in that kit, representing the community that helped shape me as a rider, made the victory even more meaningful. Overall, I ended the event with three national titles, two silver and three bronze medals. Nationals pushed me in every way, and I&#8217;m proud of how far I&#8217;ve come this season&#8212;motivated, grateful, and ready for what&#8217;s next.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$